# How to cite Diffusor. GitHub shows this as "Cite this repository", and
# Zenodo reads it when it archives a release. The version is deliberately not
# written here: it lives only in diffusor/__init__.py, and Zenodo takes it from
# the release tag. Add the concept DOI under "doi" once Zenodo has minted it.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Diffusor in published work, please cite it as below, give the version you used (it is in every exported methods block), and cite the diffusion coefficients listed in that methods block."
type: software
title: "Diffusor: diffusion chronometry with traceable coefficients and correlated uncertainties"
authors:
  - family-names: Timar
    given-names: Armin
    email: timar.armin@gmail.com
    affiliation: "Department of Earth and Planetary Sciences, Kyushu University"
repository-code: "https://github.com/ArminTimar/Diffusor"
url: "https://github.com/ArminTimar/Diffusor"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  A desktop application and Python library for diffusion chronometry. It
  solves 1-D diffusion problems analytically and numerically, carries a
  registry of published diffusion coefficients for thirteen minerals, each
  with its equation, calibration range and the place in the source where the
  numbers were read, fits diffusion times to measured or image-derived
  profiles, and propagates uncertainties by Monte Carlo while keeping
  temperature, oxygen fugacity and the Arrhenius parameters correlated.
keywords:
  - diffusion chronometry
  - geospeedometry
  - magma residence time
  - volcanology
  - petrology
  - Monte Carlo
